00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,120
Usalit! Usalit! Usalit!

249
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:23,717
I'm telling!

250
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,860
I'm telling!

251
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:27,260
You can count on your hero!

252
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,680
Is he awesome or what? Ha ha!

253
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:32,938
Gingory, you're such a stand-up guy.

254
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:34,377
I can't believe it.

255
00:15:34,460 --> 00:15:36,777
He's even nice to these little bug people.

256
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:38,625
What do you do against Robots?

257
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,980
Uh, bugs. In a good way.

258
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,080
Oh, no problem, Bing!

259
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,820
One question. Huh?

260
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,037
Who is that woman fighting
out there in the ring?

261
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,337
The crowd seems to hate her.

262
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:52,937
But judging by their jeers,
she's related to the former king.

263
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:56,360
Is there something we don't
know about the Rick dynasty?

264
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:58,520
There's nothing I don't know!

265
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:04,200
It happened ten years ago.

266
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:07,497
King Rick lost the support of his citizens

267
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:10,420
in a sudden tragedy that struck one night.

268
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:15,980
He fought for his people until the
end, but that story has been lost.

269
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:18,737
Riku's entire family can go to hell!

270
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,120
I don't blame them.

271
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:23,576
The citizens don't know what
really happened that day.

272
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:28,337
I'm sorry.

273
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:29,660
It's my fault.

274
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:32,220
I failed to protect your mother.

275
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,237
After he took control of the kingdom,

276
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:38,160
Doflamingo tried to erase
King Riku's bloodline.

277
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:42,597
But I took Rebecca away and
went into hiding with her.

278
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:45,320
Thus, she was able to grow into adulthood.

279
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:54,637
Eventually, we were discovered, and Doflamingo
decided to put her on public display!

280
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:56,657
I swear,

281
00:16:56,740 --> 00:17:01,097
I will restore the people's faith in King
Rick and I will protect Rebecca from harm,

282
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:03,397
even if I have to give my life to do it.

283
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:07,697
That is why we fight to
put an end to this—who

284
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:14,477
are

285
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:15,390
you?

286
00:17:15,473 --> 00:17:16,303
you

287
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:17,740
A failure.

288
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:20,492
A soldier who couldn't complete his duty.

289
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:22,260
I let her die.

290
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:30,900
For as long as I live, I'll never
forget what happened that day.

291
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:37,560
But Rebecca has forgotten me
because I was turned into a toy.

292
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:53,977
This toy soldier is brave and true,

293
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:57,960
in the rain or in the snow
he will stay with you.

294
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
She doesn't know.

295
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:13,780
The truth is I'm Rebecca's father.

296
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,400
Both of you go to hell!

297
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:25,257
I'll do the same to you!

298
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:29,257
Watch this—Rebecca's taking advantage
of Logan being distracted and flees.

299
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:30,170
flees

300
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,980
She's scurrying across
the arena like a rat.

301
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:43,000
And rolling low, didn't give it a chance.

302
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:46,960
Blowing down the other contenders
like a field of daisies.

303
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,816
Hey, do you want to see one, Rebecca?

304
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:51,800
Fight back or die!

305
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:58,097
But you...

306
00:18:58,180 --> 00:19:02,533
Your grandpa tried to burn us down,
Rebecca, and now he's burning in hell.

307
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:09,320
She really is King Riku's granddaughter.

308
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:13,240
If what you say was true, hold it.

309
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:15,277
What were you before you transformed?

310
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:20,037
I mean, if you're her father, and
her grandfather is the king...

311
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:22,700
Everything began on that night.

312
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:24,580
Answer my question!

313
00:19:24,980 --> 00:19:26,817
Are you a prince or something, huh?

314
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:30,957
Well, when I think about it,
the signs came before that.

315
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:35,520
It truly began when a woman named
Monet came to work at the palace.

316
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:38,020
Oh, her.

317
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,420
That's the bird lady, isn't it?

318
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:48,400
In only a decade, the whole
kingdom has been transformed.

319
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:51,300
Its people as well.

320
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,440
Hey, what happened here?

321
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,117
Some pirates were starting a ruckus,

322
00:19:56,200 --> 00:20:00,671
but the royal army ran them out so they
didn't cause much damage in the end.

323
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:08,080
My gosh, we've gone two weeks
without an inch of rain.

324
00:20:08,300 --> 00:20:12,900
Yeah, still, the flowers never
wilt, even now. Why's that?

325
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:15,317
It's thanks to the fairies, of course.

326
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:18,557
No matter how dry it gets, they
always protect the flowers.

327
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,620
I want more! I'm hungry!

328
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,937
If you have strength enough
to shout, you won't starve.

329
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:24,850
Huh?

330
00:20:24,933 --> 00:20:29,097
No matter how poor we might feel at
times, there's never war here, you know?

331
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:33,080
And peace is the most important
thing of all, don't you think?

332
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:41,740
In 800 years of the Rick dynasty, never
once was Dressrosa embroiled in war.

333
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,860
Goodness, that is remarkable.

334
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,560
Yes, almost a miracle.

335
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:50,020
Until our peace was destroyed by him.

336
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:58,300
Suddenly he descended upon the palace,
dancing in the darkness like a knight.

337
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,500
Halt! Who's there?

338
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:07,320
What the hell do you want?

339
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:12,280
My name is Don Quixote do Flamingo.

340
00:21:12,860 --> 00:21:17,625
I have heard troubling tales of a pirate
named Don Quixote wreaking havoc nearby.

341
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,278
Well, you were right to be troubled.

342
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:22,380
Though that's only the half of it.

343
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:27,600
Did you know my ancestors, the Don
Quixote family, once ruled this kingdom?

344
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:33,300
Even if you've forgotten, I have not.

345
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:36,680
Thus, I've returned to
take my place as your king!

346
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:41,397
I know about the havoc you
wreaked by stealing heavenly

347
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:44,715
tributes before they could
reach the Celestial Dragons,

348
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:48,560
and how you became a warlord
by blackmailing the government.

349
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,640
What can I say?

350
00:21:52,860 --> 00:21:54,917
Poor saps don't know what to do with me.

351
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:59,097
You can't threaten someone who's not
afraid of the Celestial Dragons, after all.

352
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:02,840
Anyway, since you know what I'm
about, let's cut to the chase.

353
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:07,577
I'll sell you this kingdom
for, say, ten billion berries?

354
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:09,880
You'd sell me my own kingdom?

355
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,817
As a courtesy.

356
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:15,841
I could also take it by force if
you don't want to accept my offer!

357
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:20,057
To avoid bloodshed, I would happily pay?

358
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:21,837
If I could, that is.

359
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:25,457
But ten billion berries
is far more than I have.

360
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:26,420
Is it?

361
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:30,257
You have until sunrise, so I'd get moving.

362
00:22:30,340 --> 00:22:32,517
You can't get outside help.

363
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:34,417
This is to test your worth as a king,

364
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:37,857
and you can't tell your
people about me or our deal.

365
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:41,317
If you don't like your
odds, then fight me,

366
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:44,877
but I'll warn you: even if
you win it won't be pretty.

367
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:49,117
Your people will be bathed in carnage.

368
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:52,060
Choose well, your majesty.

369
00:22:57,900 --> 00:22:59,397
The man is a criminal.

370
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,517
A war would be justified, my lord.

371
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:04,777
Enough fighting to kill is not the answer.

372
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:07,997
We must never lose sight of
what it means to be human,

373
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:10,877
but sir, we could never
collect that much money.

374
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,937
Few of our citizens are wealthy,

375
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:17,057
and no one has nearly that much
besides the Don Quixote family.

376
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:21,897
Abandoned Dress Rosa, our kingdom
has not engaged in war in 800 years.

377
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:24,100
That fact is proof of our humanity.

378
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:25,840
You are not a beast.

379
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:27,100
We don't kill.

380
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:29,540
I will not allow it. Listen up.

381
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:31,096
We have little time.

382
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:33,597
Split up and lead to different villages.

383
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:36,562
Collect the 10 billion
from all over the kingdom.

384
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:40,557
If you can't, the Threlso
will be ruled by pirates.

385
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,405
I fear this won't be pleasant.

386
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,430
We'll

387
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:48,377
lose the trust of our citizens when we
demand their money, but bear it till morning.

388
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:52,517
When everything is settled, I will do
everything in my power to make it up to them.

389
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:56,097
This is the only We can't use
trickery to get out of this.

390
00:23:56,180 --> 00:24:00,597
Every last berry counts—the fate of our
nation is resting on your shoulders!

391
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:01,510
It's

392
00:24:08,260 --> 00:24:10,177
in the army, it's awfully late!

393
00:24:10,260 --> 00:24:11,090
It's

394
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:16,270
an emergency.

395
00:24:16,353 --> 00:24:17,260
Listen, I

396
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:20,617
need you to fight every last berry in
town and bring them here immediately!

397
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,060
immediately Huh?

398
00:24:22,420 --> 00:24:23,857
Whoa, whoa, what's going on?

399
00:24:23,940 --> 00:24:26,657
What do you think the king is
going to say when he hears of this?

400
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:29,660
We're here on orders from the king.

401
00:24:30,300 --> 00:24:31,130
Hurry!

402
00:24:31,213 --> 00:24:33,660
There's no time left
to explain. Just do it!

403
00:24:33,860 --> 00:24:35,272
Have faith in King Rick!

404
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:37,793
Don't ask questions and bring the money!

405
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,300
Please, listen to me!

406
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:42,000
This is too fishy.

407
00:24:42,980 --> 00:24:43,820
It's hopeless.

408
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:46,826
Who would agree to such
an outlandish request?

409
00:24:48,080 --> 00:24:49,757
The video transponder snail?

410
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:51,857
People of Dressrosa.

411
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:52,840
It's King Rick!

412
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:54,437
He'll settle this mess!

413
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:59,400
I know this is rather sudden, and it must
seem quite odd, but please hear my plea.

414
00:25:00,140 --> 00:25:04,140
I need to borrow all of your money,
and I need to do so immediately.

415
00:25:04,740 --> 00:25:09,093
It is with great regret that I cannot
offer you a reason for this request.

416
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:13,120
The king is begging? King Rick?

417
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,030
Why?

418
00:25:15,113 --> 00:25:16,292
This doesn't make sense.

419
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,367
It came out of nowhere, too.

420
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:21,020
My lord, no.

421
00:25:21,280 --> 00:25:23,120
Raise your head. Stop it.

422
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:25,617
You have to show some
dignity as our leader.

423
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:26,530
That's enough.

424
00:25:26,880 --> 00:25:27,710
Stand up.

425
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:28,720
This is mad.

426
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:30,557
Think of the history books.

427
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:34,157
Every descendant of yours will be
ashamed of this crowd's indignity.

428
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:37,475
Oblating yourself, you'll
turn us into a laughingstock.

429
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:40,680
King Rick, do you think this is a joke?

430
00:25:41,020 --> 00:25:43,240
I would sacrifice anything for this.

431
00:25:43,540 --> 00:25:44,880
I don't care.

432
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:46,070
Curse my pride.

433
00:25:46,153 --> 00:25:51,041
I'd chop off my arms and legs, if that's
what it would take to keep my kingdom safe.

434
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:54,020
Listen, tank.

435
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:59,660
If things go wrong tonight, I'll
bear the burden and kill Doflamingo.

436
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:01,240
Surely not.

437
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:02,400
You can't.

438
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:06,000
I trust you.

439
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,160
Do your best.

440
00:26:10,220 --> 00:26:13,637
He put his faith, his life, in my hands.

441
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:14,740
Come on!

442
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:16,397
What is everyone waiting for?

443
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:19,020
Let's go get that money! Yeah, guys!

444
00:26:19,220 --> 00:26:20,437
The king's a good man!

445
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:23,417
If he needs our help that badly,
we don't need to question why.

446
00:26:23,500 --> 00:26:25,137
Yeah, he must have a reason.

447
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:26,597
Don't worry about it now.

448
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:29,180
Everyone, bring out your money! No, run!

449
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:56,920
King Rick, your virtue may save us.

450
00:26:58,520 --> 00:26:59,540
Take it.

451
00:27:00,120 --> 00:27:00,950
Thank you.

452
00:27:03,740 --> 00:27:05,080
I was a fool.

453
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,757
The people of this nation
share the same kindness

454
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:10,517
the Rick family has shown
them for eight centuries.

455
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:12,420
This is a wonderful kingdom.

456
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:14,780
Surely it can be saved!

457
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,320
Thank you!

458
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:19,677
We need to hurry back to the palace!

459
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:20,936
Hope this is enough!

460
00:27:21,020 --> 00:27:21,961
Full speed, men!

461
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:23,350
Captain Tank!

462
00:27:23,433 --> 00:27:24,337
Seems the king went to...

463
00:27:24,420 --> 00:27:25,250
Sivio!

464
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:27,346
It's on the screen right now!

465
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:33,430
King Rick!

466
00:27:33,513 --> 00:27:36,120
You didn't have to come
all this way! We got it!

467
00:27:36,820 --> 00:27:37,650
Run away!

468
00:27:38,660 --> 00:27:39,620
King Rick!

469
00:27:39,860 --> 00:27:42,277
I don't know what's happening,
but we're all here to help out.

470
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,772
We trust you completely.

471
00:27:44,060 --> 00:27:45,140
Get away!

472
00:27:47,420 --> 00:27:49,680
King Rick, what's wrong?

473
00:28:05,080 --> 00:28:05,910
Survive!

474
00:28:19,620 --> 00:28:21,140
Stop it!

475
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:22,800
I'm begging you!

476
00:28:23,100 --> 00:28:27,060
King Rick, please wait!
What are you doing? Go!

477
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:30,660
Stay away from me, or
I'm going to hurt you!

478
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:34,320
Soldiers too?

479
00:28:36,460 --> 00:28:39,980
My body is moving on its own!

480
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,120
My lord!

481
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:44,357
I don't...

482
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:45,360
understand!

483
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,357
Oh, Rick.

484
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:55,860
What a naughty king you are.

485
00:28:56,460 --> 00:28:58,401
The knights steal young soldiers.

486
00:28:58,580 --> 00:29:00,357
Don't just stand there gawking.

487
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:02,146
Why don't you join the dance?

488
00:29:06,260 --> 00:29:07,460
Parasite string!

489
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,657
Now the soldiers are
cutting people down too.

490
00:29:12,740 --> 00:29:14,080
No.

491
00:29:16,140 --> 00:29:16,970
Captain.

492
00:29:17,053 --> 00:29:17,883
Help me.

493
00:29:17,966 --> 00:29:21,017
Why are you doing this, King Rick?

494
00:29:21,100 --> 00:29:23,260
He was such a kind man before.

495
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:27,857
Is there something
we've done to anger you?

496
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:29,957
What could I possibly say?

497
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:31,877
Nothing can justify this.

498
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:32,817
We're done.

499
00:29:32,900 --> 00:29:34,380
The kingdom is finished.

500
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:37,740
We fell right into Doflamingo's trap.

501
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:40,137
The king's lost his mind.

502
00:29:40,220 --> 00:29:41,977
Everyone, run for your lives.

503
00:29:42,060 --> 00:29:43,000
No more, stop.

504
00:29:43,740 --> 00:29:47,917
Hey, hey, can we do it
already, please? Go-fi.

505
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:49,617
Now, now.

506
00:29:49,700 --> 00:29:52,137
We can't rush things.

507
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:56,657
I need them trembling with
fear in the depths of despair.

508
00:29:56,740 --> 00:30:00,757
And when this kingdom hates
King Rick with all its heart?

509
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:04,320
That's when the heroes
can appear! I'm here.
